# Normalize line endings so a checkout on Windows does not rewrite every file.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Linguist overrides.
#
# Scope note, because the obvious motive for a file like this is to make the
# language bar say something flattering. Only genuinely vendored, generated or
# documentation paths are marked below. Real dashboard source is NOT marked
# `linguist-detectable=false`, and here is the measurement behind that decision:
# excluding tests and vendored code from BOTH sides, the dashboard is
# ~1,358 KB of TypeScript against ~943 KB of Rust in the control plane. GitHub
# reporting TypeScript first is therefore accurate. Suppressing real source to
# change that would be making the repository host misreport the repository,
# which is the exact failure mode the rest of this project is organised against
# (see README "Project Status & Limitations"). If the language bar should say
# Rust, the honest route is a smaller dashboard or a bigger control plane.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# shadcn/ui primitives are copied in by the shadcn CLI, not authored here.
# That is how shadcn distributes: the components land in your tree verbatim.
nextjs/src/components/ui/** linguist-vendored

# Generated API contracts — `make gen-openapi` / `make gen-schemas` write these.
contracts/** linguist-generated

# Generated documentation pages. Editing these by hand is a CI failure:
# `make eval-health-check` regenerates and diffs eval-health.md, and
# observability/genai_mapping.py owns otel-genai-mapping.md.
docs/eval-health.md linguist-generated
docs/otel-genai-mapping.md linguist-generated
examples/demo/TRANSCRIPT.md linguist-generated

# Prose, not code.
docs/** linguist-documentation
*.md linguist-documentation

# Lockfiles carry no authorship.
uv.lock linguist-generated
nextjs/package-lock.json linguist-generated
